      },
      "worked": "The outer logarithm requires $\\log_3(x^2)>0$, so $x^2>1$.\n$$\\begin{align*}\n\\log_3(x^2)&=2^2\\\\\n\\log_3(x^2)&=4\\\\\nx^2&=3^4\\\\\nx^2&=81\\\\\nx&=\\pm9\n\\end{align*}$$\nBoth values satisfy $x^2>1$ and give $\\log_2\\bigl(\\log_3(81)\\bigr)=\\log_2(4)=2$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
